  "releaseNotes": "WebSocket:\n      - Removed all non‑span overloads across protocol, client, server, and session; core API is now fully span‑based for zero‑copy performance.\n      - Simplified send pipeline: no persistent send buffers, frames are built on demand and returned to pool immediately.\n      - Receive pipeline retains a single state machine for frame parsing, ensuring correct handling of fragmentation, masking, and control opcodes.\n      - Unified frame builder for text, binary, ping, pong, and close frames with consistent opcode handling and minimal allocations.\n      - Cleaned up masking logic: client masking preserved with safe locking, server path fully lock‑free.\n      - Reduced API surface and removed redundant helpers, keeping WebSocket core minimal, fast, and consistent with the rest of the engine.",
